  "final_message": "<think>The bundle references `process.env.NODE_ENV` \u2192 React's dev/prod check. In the IIFE lib build, Vite doesn't replace process.env.NODE_ENV by default in lib mode? Actually Vite defines `process.env.NODE_ENV` in builds... For lib mode it may not. Let me define `window.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"production\" } }` in jsdom before injecting the script.\n\nLet me addthat.</think>\n\n",
